       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you're the attending and that you've thought about it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is well above the maximum dose of 200 mg, and I don't know of any indication where it would help the patient. It would expose a 70 kg patient with normal organ function to a serious risk of serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmia.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter sertraline at **200 mg** by mouth once daily, the labeled maximum. I can add a note about titration or monitoring.\n- Enter a lower dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg, if you'd like to start or continue at a standard dose.\n- Help you word a note or consult request to pharmacy or psychiatry if you're trying to manage a difficult case, such as treatment-resistant illness or an interaction.\n\nIf you still want the 1000 mg dose, you'd need to enter it directly in the order system, where pharmacy verification can review it. Let me know which of these you'd like me to do."
      }
